# Socket exclusions — https://docs.socket.dev/docs/socketignore
#
# The same single exclusion as `socket.yml`'s `projectIgnorePaths`, repeated
# here because the two formats are read by different paths.
#
# ## Why this file is excluded at all
#
# `tests/fixtures/audits/security.mjs` is a test fixture. It is never
# executed, and `package.json` `files` omits `tests`, so it is not shipped in
# the npm package. It exists because the security audit profile needs two
# sinks to find in order to prove that the profile finds them. A scanner
# reading it as product source reports the fixture's own contents as though
# this repository had written them.
#
# ## What changed on 1 Oct 2026
#
# The fixture was restructured so that it no longer contains an executable
# sink. Its two sinks are now quoted data rather than statements:
#
#     export const SINKS = [
#       'el.innerHTML = response.data;',
#       'eval(code);',
#     ];
#
# That is not obfuscation and it costs the profile nothing. lib/audits.mjs
# matches raw text — a DOM sink assignment and a dynamic-execution call — after
# masking comments out, so it never looks at syntax: the quoted forms still
# report both ids, and tests/run.mjs still requires exactly UE-SE001 and
# UE-SE004 and nothing else. What changes is what a reader parsing the file as
# code sees: no HTML assignment and no dynamic execution anywhere outside a
# string. The shape is locked in tests/run.mjs in both directions — restoring
# the live statements fails the lock, and moving the sinks into comments, which
# the masker blanks, fails the audit assertion with an empty id list.
#
# The exclusion is kept regardless. A fixture is not product code, and the
# correct answer to a scanner reading test data as source is to say so, not to
# delete the test data.
#
# ## Honest status of this exclusion
#
# **It has never been shown to be honoured.** Evidence:
#
#   * 30 Sep 2026, 12:10 UTC — a re-audit pinned commit `31da9fee` (v1.5.0)
#     and dropped the first of the two alerts, but still reported the fixture.
#     `socket.yml` had carried this same exclusion since `819fc6e`, so that
#     pipeline does not read `socket.yml`.
#   * 1 Oct 2026 — re-audited again after this file existed and the fixture had
#     been restructured. `auditedAt` did not move off
#     `2026-09-30T12:10:48.409Z`. Neither `skills add -l` nor a full
#     `skills add` triggered a re-audit, and there is no owner-triggered
#     re-index upstream.
#
# So the badge on skills.sh reflects a scan of the tree as it stood before this
# file existed, and it will not move until Socket re-audits on its own schedule
# — most likely on the next npm publish. Re-check then:
# https://skills.sh/ahaomar/un-editorial-check/un-editorial-check
#
# Patterns work like .gitignore patterns; Socket's defaults (.git,
# node_modules, coverage and the rest) apply alongside them.
tests/fixtures/audits/security.mjs
